b/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186528520 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528956 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186528592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528956 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186528598 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528956 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186528794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528956 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186528875 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528956 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528956 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528956 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186528520 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528956 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "20580d7d-28aa-5c7c-a048-784d0bfa2d4b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528960 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186528560 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528960 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186528567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528960 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186528849 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528960 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186528852 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528960 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186528903 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528960 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528960 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528960 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186528849 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528960 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "255a02e5-2e2c-5989-905e-69f5223274a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529139 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186528960 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529139 #edb/ref 1069 "q-142472" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529139 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529139 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and  $det(A)=-1?$ \n\nI. $A$ is **not** invertible\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=3$\n\nIII. $A$ has $4$ pivot columns" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529139 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "74f4be02-4fe9-5741-a4d1-7268f77a2f5f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529139 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{3} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=3=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed,   a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ Since here we have $det(A)=-1\\ne 0,$ our matrix $A$ must be invertible.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, by the invertible matrix theorem\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{rank}(A)=3.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $\\text{rank}(A)=3$,  it must be $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=3$ which, in turn, means that  $A$ has $3$ pivot columns, not $4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529191 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186528956 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529191 #edb/ref 1069 "q-141342" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529191 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529191 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)\\ne 0,$ then  $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\text{Null}(A)$ has no basis\n\nII. $A$ is **not** invertible\n\nIII. All columns of $A$ are pivot columns" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529191 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f1d7f6a4-6114-5671-a52c-7df48bee5e24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529191 #edb/ref 1074 "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately. \n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Null}(A)$ has no basis.* $\\,\\times $ \n\nSince $\\text{nullity}(A)\\ne 0,$ we have $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}$ which, in turn, means that $\\text{Null}(A)$ must have a basis.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $A$ is **not** invertible.* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, by the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(A)\\ne 0,$ we must have that $A$ is **not** invertible.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.* $\\,\\times $\n\nSince $A$ is not invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{n},$ which means that not all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529197 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0a7d2e71-2df5-5616-a66c-1039ae6b7480" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529197 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186272348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529199 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186529197 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529199 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2a21ddf3-d51f-5117-8439-7fd92a4b2b2d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529199 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186529139 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529200 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186529199 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529200 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "94778ac8-3dd7-5564-88c5-443046b2e6fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529200 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186529191 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529203 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186529200 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529203 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cb8b82a3-c3e9-567b-8dbd-19ce7dce93de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529203 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186272238 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529204 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186529203 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529204 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e46ea0a8-4991-5f8c-a308-9bc68c5b0d80" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529204 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186329820 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
